          4 OK         Move 2: the old ancestors were REMOVED, not merely supplemented                                                                                                                                          0 of the 4 replaced pairs -- (AGENCY,LMA), (AGENCY,HAZ_WASTE), (WSA,LMA), (WSA,HAZ_WASTE) -- are still LIVE after LMA moved to the root. Anything but 0 is the incremental-algorithm defect: a scope grant at AGENCY would still reach a program that is no longer beneath it, with no symptom anywhere but in an authorization decision.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
          4 OK         Move 2: the replaced pairs were SOFT-deleted and kept                                                                                                                                                    4 of 4 replaced pairs carry IsDeleted = 1 after the move. Conventions non-negotiable 3: auth.uspRebuildTenantClosure has no hard delete, so a re-parenting leaves the old shape on record rather than erasing it. A count below 4 means rows went missing.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
          4 OK         Move 2: the new ancestor sets are complete and no larger                                                                                                                                                 LMA has 2 live ancestor pair(s), 2 expected (itself and ROOT); HAZ_WASTE has 3, 3 expected (itself, LMA, ROOT). Too many means the old pairs are still there; too few means an ancestor was lost and a legitimate scope grant would stop reaching the tenant.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           
          4 OK         Round trip: the restored closure is identical to the baseline                                                                                                                                            0 row(s) differ between the live closure before move 1 and after move 3, compared on (ancestor, descendant, depth) in both directions. 0 means three re-parentings and their inverse left the closure exactly as it was. auditModifiedDateUtc is deliberately NOT compared: those rows were genuinely rewritten, and the audit trail is supposed to show it.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            
          4 OK         Restore: the retired pair was resurrected in place                                                                                                                                                       1 row(s) for (AGENCY, LMA) after the restore, 1 expected, of which 1 live at depth 1, 1 expected. The pair was soft-deleted by move 2 and undeleted by move 3 -- the same row throughout, which is what keeps the movement on record.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
          4 OK         A second rebuild changes nothing at all                                                                                                                                                                  0 row(s) differ between the closure after move 3 and after an immediate second rebuild, compared on (ancestor, descendant, depth, IsDeleted, auditModifiedDateUtc). 0 means the MERGE touched no row -- not merely that it arrived at the same answer. A rebuild that rewrote every row to the value it already held would pass a count check and destroy the audit trail.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
          4 OK         Untouched applications: VARIANT1                                                                                                                                                                         SUM (Depth + 1) = 7, live pairs = 7, retired pairs = 0. Nothing in this tree was moved, so retired must be 0. The rebuild is whole-table and parameterless, which is exactly why a test that only checked the tree it moved would miss this. Both pair counts are restricted to descendants auth.vwTenantHierarchy can see: a soft-deleted tenant keeps its live pairs on purpose, and counting them here would report the design as damage.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            
          4 OK         Untouched applications: VARIANT3                                                                                                                                                                         SUM (Depth + 1) = 26, live pairs = 26, retired pairs = 0. Nothing in this tree was moved, so retired must be 0. The rebuild is whole-table and parameterless, which is exactly why a test that only checked the tree it moved would miss this. Both pair counts are restricted to descendants auth.vwTenantHierarchy can see: a soft-deleted tenant keeps its live pairs on purpose, and counting them here would report the design as damage.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
          4 OK         Every live tenant is still usable after three movements                                                                                                                                                  0 of 25 tenant(s) read as unusable. The population is every tenant auth.vwTenantHierarchy can see whose own IsActive is 1 and none of whose ancestors is inactive, so anything but 0 means a rebuild dropped a depth-0 self row and locked those tenants out with 50021. A tenant deliberately disabled by another test -- 080 keeps one, to probe 50021 -- is legitimately unusable and is not evidence of anything, which is why the population is not simply IsDeleted = 0.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
