          4 OK         A cycle makes the rebuild fail loudly                                                                                                                                                                    auth.uspRebuildTenantClosure raised error 530 on a two-node cycle; 530 expected -- "maximum recursion 100 has been exhausted". NULL means it SUCCEEDED, which would mean the MERGE wrote a closure for a tree that has no valid closure. OPTION (MAXRECURSION 100) is what makes this an error rather than a rebuild that runs until tempdb is full.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
          4 OK         The failed rebuild left the closure untouched                                                                                                                                                            27 live pair(s) before the cycle, 27 after the failure and the restore. The rebuild does its whole MERGE in one transaction and its CATCH rolls back, so a rebuild that cannot finish must leave the previous closure intact rather than a partial one -- a partially rebuilt closure is an authorization table with rows missing.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      
          4 OK         The failure was recorded in logs.ExecutionLog                                                                                                                                                            Latest unsuccessful row for [auth].[uspRebuildTenantClosure] carries ErrorNumber 530 and ReCreatedAfterRollback 0; 530 and 0 expected. 0 because the start row was opened in autocommit BEFORE the transaction, so the procedure's own ROLLBACK could not destroy it and the CATCH took the MATCHED branch. Rule 8 on a real failure, not a probe's.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
Cycle: refused with 530, closure left intact, failure recorded. Phase 1 exit criterion 2 satisfied.
